### Pruebas manuales (VS Code "REST Client" o IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Reemplaza @gw por la URL de API Gateway (o http://localhost si pruebas directo contra los puertos) y @token por el JWT de Cognito
@gw = https://TU_API_ID.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
@token = PEGAR_AQUI_EL_JWT

### 0. Salud (publico, sin token)
GET {{gw}}/api/catalog/health

### 1. Sin token -> 401 (API Gateway rechaza)
GET {{gw}}/api/orders

### 2. Catalogo
GET {{gw}}/api/catalog/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Crear pedido (CLIENTE/OPERADOR/ADMIN) -> evento a RabbitMQ (topic) + SNS
POST {{gw}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"items":[{"productId":1,"quantity":2}]}

### 4. Aceptar pedido (ADMIN/OPERADOR): reserva stock por REST en catalog-service + ticket por cola 'tickets'
PUT {{gw}}/api/orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"ACEPTADO"}

### 5. Ticket generado de forma asincrona (esperar ~1 s)
GET {{gw}}/api/orders/1/ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Bitacora escrita por el consumidor SQS (requiere AWS_ENABLED=true)
GET {{gw}}/api/orders/1/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Alertas de stock bajo (cola 'inventario')
GET {{gw}}/api/catalog/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ================= rabbit-admin-service (solo ADMIN) =================

### 8. Crear cola (con su DLQ)
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"pedidos360.reportes.q","durable":true,"withDeadLetter":true}

### 9. Validacion: nombre vacio -> 400
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":""}

### 10. Crear exchange
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/exchanges
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"pedidos360.reportes","type":"DIRECT"}

### 11. Crear binding
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/bindings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"exchange":"pedidos360.reportes","queue":"pedidos360.reportes.q","routingKey":"reporte.diario"}

### 12. Listar colas / exchanges / bindings
GET {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{gw}}/api/rabbit/exchanges
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{gw}}/api/rabbit/bindings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Estado de una cola (mensajes / consumidores)
GET {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues/pedidos360.notificaciones.q.dlq
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. DLQ por mensaje corrupto (JSON invalido -> NACK -> pedidos360.notificaciones.q.dlq)
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"exchange":"pedidos360.topic","routingKey":"pedido.creado","payload":"esto no es json"}

### 15. DLQ por fallo recuperable (3 reintentos y luego DLQ): correo del dominio fail.pedidos360.test
POST {{gw}}/api/rabbit/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"exchange":"pedidos360.topic","routingKey":"pedido.creado","payload":"{\"eventId\":\"demo-1\",\"type\":\"PedidoCreado\",\"version\":1,\"orderId\":999,\"customerEmail\":\"x@fail.pedidos360.test\",\"status\":\"CREADO\",\"total\":1000,\"items\":[]}"}

### 16. Vaciar una cola / eliminar cola y su DLQ
DELETE {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues/pedidos360.reportes.q/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{gw}}/api/rabbit/queues/pedidos360.reportes.q?withDlq=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Eliminar binding y exchange
DELETE {{gw}}/api/rabbit/bindings?exchange=pedidos360.reportes&queue=pedidos360.reportes.q&routingKey=reporte.diario
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{gw}}/api/rabbit/exchanges/pedidos360.reportes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
